From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amphoze <184834775+Amphoze@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:49:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] query: one bounded, audited path to postgres-meta
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every statement and every type generation of the server goes through one function. It takes
the connection string from the request's project — the read-only one whenever the member's
role is read_only, whatever the call site asks — waits for a slot of the project's
postgres-meta instance, writes the audit record and sends nothing when that fails, and asks
the instance the control plane names with two headers of its own: nothing a caller hands in
is passed on. The call has a deadline and the answer a byte bound.

Slots: a bounded number of calls in flight per instance and per project, granted to the
waiting projects in turn; a project is given a further slot only while two are free; a wait
is bounded in time and in places. A request keeps its slot until its response has been taken
by the client, piece by piece, until the client has gone, or until the hand-over has lasted
its own bound, when the body is cut. The request guard hands every response over this way.

When the database does not take the login, what is kept of the project is dropped and the
control plane asked once; the call is sent again only if it now names another string.

The address of postgres-meta is the node's setting, two instances, read in this module
alone and checked when the server starts; upstream's address constant and its last helper
are gone.
